{"id": "EUVD-2026-86750", "enisaUuid": "8d73dd4c-7b4b-3408-bd85-a6a330275576", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nio_uring/rw: end write accounting from ->ki_complete\n\nCommit b000145e9907 moved both the fsnotify calls and the write\naccounting out of the kiocb completion handler and into the\nio_req_rw_complete() task_work. However, only the fsnotify part actually\nneeded to move as it may sleep. Ending the write accounting is just a\npercpu_up_read() on the superblock writers sem.\n\nDeferring it is a problem, because it makes dropping SB_FREEZE_WRITE\nprotection depend on the ring owner getting to running task_work. But\nthe task may be blocked in freeze_super(), causing it to never get to\nthat:\n\n  task                             io-wq worker\n  --------------------------------------------------------------\n  io_write()\n    io_kiocb_start_write()         (takes sb_writers, hidden from\n                                    lockdep by __sb_writers_release)\n    write_iter() -> -EIOCBQUEUED\n  ioctl(FS_IOC_SHUTDOWN)\n    bdev_freeze()\n      freeze_super()\n        percpu_down_write()        <- waits for the reader above\n                                   io_write()\n                                     kiocb_start_write()\n                                       percpu_down_read()  <- queued\n                                                              behind the\n                                                              writer\n  <bio completes>\n    io_complete_rw()\n      queues io_req_rw_complete()  <- never runs, task is in D state\n\nEnd the write from io_complete_rw() instead, and leave only the fsnotify\ncalls in task_work.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:30", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ed1cead97afb9c398bd7ab344a3c1ee34ab73af9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/696459029f3b65c070c91b729478475582f1dcdf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc580cee4dfa2ec9099c30ecbd4d804cbb996432", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/055d43a1233edbd80e558889258105ce63051bcd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/796aa0547557e63338657ed1c487906f9fac4c73"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97619", "GHSA-rr3w-gg4f-957r"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c6c9922-b3bc-3784-84e0-fce82e97d559", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "0f8b2cbe-5d78-32b4-9882-de2cab6ef74e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1"}, {"id": "1c5dfa63-c9f0-34ef-88cd-b7ad90b096d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ea2e6286e3e89a115ae554e20ba9aec2b2e1ddff"}, {"id": "293d8121-2d71-3822-9c17-4cc1e7158a09", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "2ce2f779-4a50-3fd0-803f-836e2672c649", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "2ea938a9-1044-3daf-921d-40216d0fe8c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b000145e9907809406d8164c3b2b8861d95aecd1 <ed1cead97afb9c398bd7ab344a3c1ee34ab73af9"}, {"id": "4d32d6f8-75f6-3f72-a349-fd30096b228a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "5aba7df1-6d64-32a5-8736-7b246aada193", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b000145e9907809406d8164c3b2b8861d95aecd1 <696459029f3b65c070c91b729478475582f1dcdf"}, {"id": "7da1326f-e25c-33c3-bc2a-98056e00d4b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b000145e9907809406d8164c3b2b8861d95aecd1 <796aa0547557e63338657ed1c487906f9fac4c73"}, {"id": "818e4954-4c4b-3d53-b719-ffe3d75cec1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0.3 <6.1"}, {"id": "82053a96-9626-3584-a3f6-71f0e267a8cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.90 <5.16"}, {"id": "82e6746f-ef68-3fe8-ba42-748bf12cc70b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2a853c206e553dd9c0a55c22858fd6a446d93e15"}, {"id": "956d238b-47c3-3b43-b0fb-55b17d9caed9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.165 <5.11"}, {"id": "9b5a1a70-1af8-3eef-832f-f3ecb3ed45ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "89a410dbd0f159ddd308f19d6eb682fc753e4771"}, {"id": "a2ea76db-c108-3a65-a259-17c31d66d192", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b000145e9907809406d8164c3b2b8861d95aecd1 <055d43a1233edbd80e558889258105ce63051bcd"}, {"id": "b7d25ddb-22bb-3e64-8094-5307dea8aa52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ef1d91e3-7e87-39e6-9d1c-b4b7dbc50e94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b000145e9907809406d8164c3b2b8861d95aecd1 <cc580cee4dfa2ec9099c30ecbd4d804cbb996432"}, {"id": "f56a5cbf-7bda-3515-b2b6-dfd83173efdf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6b16d9a3-a97c-300b-aebd-470aa75b1a12", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}